  "body": "**What.** Make `check_numbers.py`'s `formula_refit` item independent of the machine's BLAS. Do the refit of README \"The formula\" in a BLAS-free way: exact rationals, mpmath at high precision, or a QR written out in Python. Then the \"refit within 1e-9 of the stored \u0394\" item measures the formula, not the linear algebra library. Found by win in #179.\n\n**Why.** On win, `check_numbers.py --selftest` fails this item with both its old stack (venv-t151: delta_fit_range 9.4e-9, delta_80 3.2e-7) and the Python 3.14 one (3.1e-9). The refit is ill-conditioned: its coefficients move up to 2% with the library stack and 4% with the OpenBLAS kernel. So a 1e-9 tolerance on a BLAS-dependent least squares cannot hold on every runner. AGENTS.md forbids loosening the threshold, so the computation has to become deterministic instead.\n\n**Acceptance (can fail).**\n- The new refit gives the same result to 1e-12 on the Mac, win and win2, or the differing digit is reported.\n- The item passes everywhere at the original 1e-9.\n- Its existing control, the one-unit shift of `--selftest`, still fires.\n- A planted check: a synthetic data set with a known exact fit is recovered to 1e-15.\n\n**Depends on.** #179.\n",
